					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5196</guid>
				<title>SCP-5196</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5196</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Item #: SCP-5196&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/an-image-of-scp-5196-in-containment&quot;&gt;An image of SCP-5196 in containment.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Object Class: Safe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Special Containment Procedures: SCP-5196 is to be contained in a 5x9 standard humanoid containment cell with a remote-controlled steel cage in the center of the cell. This item is restricted to personnel under Level 2 clearance. Physical contact should be restricted outside of testing purposes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Description: SCP-5196 is an inanimate humanoid object that takes the form of a golden statue with minor scratching to the front. Upon physical contact with SCP-5196, the subject (Now stated as SCP-5196-2) will be melted into a molten gold liquid that will then fuse into SCP-5196, furthermore, if an instance of SCP-5196-2 should be caught SCP-5196-2 should be brought to a high power freezing device that is able to reach -20 degrees Celcius for no less than 72 hours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Test log-0130&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Dr. Koliski [Class-D 5124, please enter the containment chamber.]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;D-5124 entered the chamber without resistance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dr. Koliski opened the cage containing SCP-5196.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dr. Koliski [Class-D 5124, please approach and make contact with SCP-5196]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;D-5124 pauses for 5 seconds then approaches SCP-5196 and places a hand onto SCP-5196&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5196-2 then begins melting into a gold liquid while screaming.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5196-2 then begins crawling to SCP-6701 then fusing with SCP-6701.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-viking&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7155529&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1608733526&quot; alt=&quot;Doctor Viking&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7155529)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-viking&quot;  &gt;Doctor Viking&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 23 Dec 2020 06:51:53 +0000</pubDate>
												<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p>Item #: SCP-5196</p> <hr /> <p><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/an-image-of-scp-5196-in-containment">An image of SCP-5196 in containment.</a><br /> Object Class: Safe</p> <hr /> <p>Special Containment Procedures: SCP-5196 is to be contained in a 5x9 standard humanoid containment cell with a remote-controlled steel cage in the center of the cell. This item is restricted to personnel under Level 2 clearance. Physical contact should be restricted outside of testing purposes.</p> <hr /> <p>Description: SCP-5196 is an inanimate humanoid object that takes the form of a golden statue with minor scratching to the front. Upon physical contact with SCP-5196, the subject (Now stated as SCP-5196-2) will be melted into a molten gold liquid that will then fuse into SCP-5196, furthermore, if an instance of SCP-5196-2 should be caught SCP-5196-2 should be brought to a high power freezing device that is able to reach -20 degrees Celcius for no less than 72 hours.</p> <hr /> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Test log-0130</span><br /> Dr. Koliski [Class-D 5124, please enter the containment chamber.]</p> <p>D-5124 entered the chamber without resistance.</p> <p>Dr. Koliski opened the cage containing SCP-5196.</p> <p>Dr. Koliski [Class-D 5124, please approach and make contact with SCP-5196]</p> <p>D-5124 pauses for 5 seconds then approaches SCP-5196 and places a hand onto SCP-5196</p> <p>SCP-5196-2 then begins melting into a gold liquid while screaming.</p> <p>SCP-5196-2 then begins crawling to SCP-6701 then fusing with SCP-6701.</p> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-viking" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7155529&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608733526" alt="Doctor Viking" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7155529)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-viking" >Doctor Viking</a></span></p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
