					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>« <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-07-2020">July 2020</a> | <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-08-2020">August 2020</a></span> | <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-09-2020">September 2020</a> »</strong></p> </div> <div style="border: 2px solid black; background-color: Moccasin;"> <p style="text-align: center;">The dynamic nature of this wiki means that linked pages might get moved, renamed, deleted, or replaced. Old news pages remain as time capsules and are not updated to account for these changes.</p> </div> <p><span style="font-size:75%;">This is a series showing off news from the site, articles from the past month<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-187416-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup>, and fan-content for you to check out and discover! Be sure to leave a comment with your thoughts!</span></p> <h4><span>Fandom Stuff</span></h4> <ul> <li>A bunch of old articles including <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-682">SCP-682</a> got new images!</li> </ul> <ul> <li>The French branch of the SCP Wiki celebrated 2000 members and 5000 articles at the same time!</li> </ul> <ul> <li>The INT SCP Discord is setting up new channels to encourage cross-branch collaboration and has started with a joint DE-IT site!</li> </ul> <ul> <li>The German (DE) Wiki has completed their rules for canon and have facilitated contribution!</li> </ul> <ul> <li>The Canon Renaissance Contest was announced!</li> </ul> <h4><span>Featured Articles</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5309">SCP-5309</a> (&quot;Stele&quot;) written by Greyve, selected by captain cold, barredowl, and dianaberry<br /> &quot;<em>I am Sisyphus.sic, a synthetic intelligence construct employed by the Department of Pataphysics.</em>&quot;</li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/substation-9">Substation 9</a> written by The Great Hippo, selected by karakatt and chiifu<br /> &quot;<em>I work for an electric company that provides power to over a dozen warehouses and manufacturing complexes.</em>&quot;</li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/uiu-file-2001-023">UIU File 2001-023</a> written by Calibri Bold, selected by Truc Linh, cluadios23, and dr wile.<br /> &quot;<em>Entity is an immense disembodied eyeball, capable of independent motion and sapient thought.&quot;</em></li> </ul> <h4><span>Reviewer's Spotlight Articles</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3393-ex">SCP-3393-EX</a> - &quot;Girlfriend&quot; by Captain Kirby, featured by Riemann</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/mission-accomplished">Mission Accomplished</a> by Weizhong, featured by forbiddenquest</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5785">SCP-5785</a> - &quot;Craptivism&quot; by Deadly Bread and Sonderance, featured by Sonderance</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/project-proposal-1994-103">Project Proposal 1994-103: &quot;A Song of Hope and Home&quot;</a> by Stormbreath, featured by cybersqyd</li> </ul> <div id="toc" class="floatright"> <div id="toc-action-bar"><a href="javascript:;" >Fold</a><a style="display: none" href="javascript:;" >Unfold</a></div> <div class="title">Table of Contents</div> <div id="toc-list"> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc0">Week of August 1st:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc1">Week of August 8th:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc2">Week of August 15th:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc3">Week of August 22nd:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc4">Fanart</a></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <p>You will notice little '📈' emojis beside some articles. That denotes SCP articles which were under 30 and tales which were under 20 when this edition of site news was posted. Give them a little love! Speaking from personal experience, the most frustrating thing that can happen to an article is not deletion, but stagnating below 20 without any comments. So try to read, vote, and comment on these articles! They're often hidden gems :)</p> <h3><span>Week of August 1st:</span></h3> <h4><span>SCPs</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5738">SCP-5738</a> (&quot;Opportunity Shackles&quot;) - The unemployment, it's terrible, isn't it? Flopmind can talk about that, they know what it is.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5271">SCP-5271</a> (&quot;there is a god, and they are a penguin&quot;) - Yeah. That's it, that's the thing. Written by chiifu.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5971">SCP-5971</a> (&quot;A Moment Where Words Don't Reach&quot;) - And if they can't reach the exit of our mouth, they can't reach for the stars. Written by RockTeethMothEyes.</li> <li>📈 <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-088-pt">SCP-088-PT</a> (&quot;This machine kills communists&quot;) - For some people, the old fights a la Pete Seeger stopped being the priority, alas. Written by Vintner, translated by INT_Translator.</li> <li>📈 <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5910">SCP-5910</a> (&quot;This is a true story.&quot;) - We're not the type of people who try to hide the truth, oh no. Story writ&#8230; told by ThisMightBeAuto.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5079">SCP-5079</a> (&quot;<strong>Isolation Reverie</strong>&quot;) - Hey, don't act like it was something new. Everyone do that. Reveries are cool. Dreamed by Grigori Karpin.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5074">SCP-5074</a> (&quot;Childhoods End, and Bubbles Burst&quot;) - <em>Say goodbye to the thrills of life / When love was good, life was bad</em>. Bubbles buried in a jungle by Tyumen.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5801">SCP-5801</a> (&quot;Snowman Heaven&quot;) - Snowmen go under the sun when they want to die. Written by FluffyDog00.</li> <li>📈 <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1329-ru-ex">SCP-1329-RU-EX</a> (&quot;A Little Big Adventure&quot;) - And this time